1
00:00:00,067 --> 00:00:02,033
Everyone says the one problem

2
00:00:02,033 --> 00:00:03,200
stopping a real

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:04,533
Iron Man suit

4
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,100
is the arc reactor.

5
00:00:06,267 --> 00:00:07,867
I ran the numbers.

6
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:08,700
It's not.

7
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:10,833
The real problem is hovering.

8
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:12,000
Hovering means pushing

9
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,700
your whole weight down

10
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,600
through the air, every second.

11
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,267
My suit burns about five kilograms

12
00:00:18,267 --> 00:00:20,600
of fuel a minute doing that.

13
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,833
Flying forward on a wing

14
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:24,400
burns less than one.

15
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,200
That's five times less.

16
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,000
So the fix isn't

17
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,600
a better power source.

18
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,400
It's wings.

19
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,400
They swing back for speed,

20
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,000
open wide to turn,

21
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
and tilt up to brake.

22
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,733
With wings, the same suit flies

23
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:40,367
for about an hour

24
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:42,367
when launched like a glider.

25
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:44,000
The reactor can wait.

26
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:44,633
Follow,

27
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:47,000
and I'll show you the test.

